@startuml
title Public recommendation — v4

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor Visitor
boundary "Browser SPA" as Browser
control "FERTO Worker" as Worker
database "D1" as D1

Visitor -> Browser: Open the site / ask for another track
Browser -> Worker: GET /api/recommendation\n[?exclude=currentTrackId]

Worker -> D1: Read live generation + cached candidate\nand artist-bucket counts

note right of D1
  Promotion materializes dense integer slots after applying
  never_recordings and rebuild_known_recordings. Like / Never compacts them
  in one serialized D1 batch (concurrent removals cannot leave slot holes);
  a stale externally-liked slot is removed lazily. Staging
  generations are never selected.
end note

alt The exclude parameter is a valid Spotify track id
  Worker -> Worker: Drop that one representative\nfor this request only
  note right of Worker
    Excluding the current track does not
    shrink candidateCount and does not
    persist: the next request can get it
    again. Invalid values are ignored.
  end note
end

Worker -> Worker: Draw an exact bucket_slot uniformly\n(artist buckets are equally likely,\nnot weighted by catalogue size)
Worker -> D1: Read that single bucket row\n(bucket_artist_id + track_count)
Worker -> Worker: Draw an exact track_slot uniformly\ninside that artist's bucket
Worker -> D1: Read that single recording row
D1 --> Worker: One representative row

note over Worker,D1 #D9EAD3
  The public path never runs COUNT, DISTINCT, or
  ORDER BY RANDOM() across the catalogue. Its D1 rows
  read stay constant as the shelf grows.
end note

Worker --> Browser: 200 JSON with exactly:\n{ recommendation: { spotify_id, title,\nartists (ordered), album_name, image_url,\nspotify_url }, candidateCount }
note over Worker #D9EAD3
  The response exposes no refresh internals and no
  internal identity (no ISRC, no recording key,
  no generation). Visitors are strictly read-only:
  there is no public write endpoint.
end note

Browser -> Browser: Render the official Spotify\ncompact embed + open.spotify.com link
Browser --> Visitor: Show the recommendation

alt Shelf empty or fully filtered
  Worker --> Browser: { recommendation: null, candidateCount }
  Browser --> Visitor: Friendly "check back soon" state
end

note over Browser,Visitor #FFF2CC
  There is no custom playback: audio plays through
  Spotify's own embedded player only.
end note

@enduml
